-- title:
--   Complete intersection gives equality of cotangent and congruence lengths
-- statement:
--   Let $\mathcal O$ be a commutative ring which is a domain and a discrete valuation ring, complete (and separated) for the adic topology of its maximal ideal, and let $T$ be a commutative local ring equipped with an $\mathcal O$-algebra structure making it finite and free as an $\mathcal O$-module. Let $\pi_T : T \to \mathcal O$ be an $\mathcal O$-algebra homomorphism. Assume the hypothesis `hCI`: there exist a natural number $n$ and a family $f : \mathrm{Fin}\,n \to \mathcal O[[X_1,\dots,X_n]]$ of power series in $n$ variables over $\mathcal O$ such that the quotient $\mathcal O[[X_1,\dots,X_n]]/(f_1,\dots,f_n)$ by the ideal generated by the range of $f$ admits an isomorphism of $\mathcal O$-algebras onto $T$ (the number of relations equals the number of variables; no condition is imposed on the constant terms of the $f_i$). The conclusion is an equality in $\mathbb N \cup \{\infty\}$ of two $\mathcal O$-module lengths: the length of the cotangent module $I/I^2$ of the ideal $I = \ker \pi_T$ equals the length of $\mathcal O$ modulo the image under $\pi_T$ of the annihilator of $\ker \pi_T$ in $T$.
--
--   This is the implication ‘complete intersection $\Rightarrow$ equality of invariants’ in the Wiles–Lenstra numerical criterion, asserting $\mathrm{length}_{\mathcal O}\Phi_T = \mathrm{length}_{\mathcal O}(\mathcal O/\eta_T)$ for the cotangent module $\Phi_T$ and congruence ideal $\eta_T$ attached to $\pi_T$; it is a statement of commutative algebra, with no modular forms or Galois representations involved. It is used, through [`AlgHom.length_cotangent_mul_eq_length_quotient_of_free`](thm.html#AlgHom.length_cotangent_mul_eq_length_quotient_of_free), in the modularity-lifting estimates for local Hecke algebras once these are known to be complete intersections.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_AlgHom_length_cotangent_eq_of_exists_presentation.lean

import Mathlib.RingTheory.Ideal.Cotangent
import Mathlib.RingTheory.Length
import Mathlib.RingTheory.DiscreteValuationRing.Basic
import Mathlib.RingTheory.MvPowerSeries.Basic
import Mathlib.RingTheory.AdicCompletion.Basic
import Mathlib.LinearAlgebra.Matrix.Determinant.Basic
import Mathlib.RingTheory.LocalRing.ResidueField.Defs
import Mathlib.RingTheory.TensorProduct.Basic
import Mathlib.RingTheory.Flat.FaithfullyFlat.Basic

set_option maxHeartbeats 4000000
set_option synthInstance.maxHeartbeats 400000
set_option backward.isDefEq.respectTransparency.types false

universe u v w x

theorem AlgHom.length_cotangent_eq_of_exists_presentation
    {𝒪 : Type u} {T : Type w}
    [CommRing 𝒪] [IsDomain 𝒪] [IsDiscreteValuationRing 𝒪] [IsAdicComplete (IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal 𝒪) 𝒪]
    [CommRing T] [IsLocalRing T] [Algebra 𝒪 T] [Module.Finite 𝒪 T] [Module.Free 𝒪 T]
    (πT : T →ₐ[𝒪] 𝒪)
    (hCI : ∃ (n : ℕ) (f : Fin n → MvPowerSeries (Fin n) 𝒪),
        Nonempty ((MvPowerSeries (Fin n) 𝒪 ⧸ Ideal.span (Set.range f)) ≃ₐ[𝒪] T)) :
    Module.length 𝒪 (RingHom.ker πT).Cotangent =
      Module.length 𝒪 (𝒪 ⧸ (RingHom.ker πT).annihilator.map πT) := by sorry
